  {
   "id": "FAM:SF-APPS-024",
   "what_failed": "DRIVE-as-BEST counter test on 44 suppression triggers",
   "why": "MDE 0.180 PPP at 80% power; observed gap -0.066 below MDE, untestable."
  },
  {
   "id": "FAM:SF-PAP-029",
   "what_failed": "Destination net rating outcome for movers",
   "why": "Underpowered after landing-spot correction; no numbers kept."
  }
 ],
 "evidence_establishes": [
  "For connectors (a broader role group that likely includes shapers), pre-move cut share positively predicts post-move role reproduction, with a modest effect (AUC 0.622) in an exploratory analysis of 92 movers (FAM:SF-CHT-057).",
  "Multiple mover-based tests on related questions have been untestable or borderline due to small sample sizes (n=19, 44, and an underpowered net-rating check), highlighting severe power limitations.",
  "The earlier work treats the cut-drive portability difference as a boundary condition, not a confirmatory result."
 ],
 "evidence_does_not_establish": [
  "Whether the cut vs drive portability effect replicates specifically in shapers, a more narrowly defined role subset.",
  "Whether the effect size would be large enough to detect with only n=24 shaper movers.",
  "Causal mechanisms separating play-type preference from other confounding factors (landing-spot quality, team system, usage change).",
  "Stability of the cut-heavy/drive-heavy classification across seasons and its measurement reliability."
 ],
 "own_inferences": [
  "The current question is a direct refinement of the exploratory CHT-057 finding, but targeting shapers reduces the sample to n=24, far below the 92 that already showed marginal power and small-sample risk.",
